    "en": {
      "summary": "Corns/calluses are thickened skin from pressure/friction. NHS: better-fitting shoes, padding, podiatry — avoid aggressive home cutting if you have diabetes or poor circulation. Emergency: spreading infection, ulcer under a corn, or black/painful ischaemic toe.",
